          "email": "nikitas.angelinas@hpe.com",
          "date": "2026-10-07 19:43:52.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "subject": "LU-20894 compat: test for core XArray not CONFIG_XARRAY_MULTI",
        "message": "LU-20894 compat: test for core XArray not CONFIG_XARRAY_MULTI\n\nLU-19179 changes removed the copy of XArray from the Lustre tree and\nrelied on the in-kernel implementation; an autoconf test was added in\ncase there was no XArray support in the kernel, but it checked for the\npresence of CONFIG_XARRAY_MULTI, which does not denote core XArray\nsupport, but an XArray feature for supporting entries which occupy\nmultiple consecutive indices in the XArray, for increased efficiency.\nThis additional multi-index functionality is not currently used by\nLustre, though, so it should not be considered a requirement.\n\nLU-19179 made the assumption that CONFIG_XARRAY_MULTI should be set in\nvirtually all distribution kernels, as it is selected by\nCONFIG_ZONE_DEVICE, which was expected to also be normally set and\nadded a configure check for CONFIG_XARRAY_MULTI, so that the build\nwould fail, just in case it isn't set. However, it seems to be\npossible to have at least some SLES 15 SP2/SP3 (probably\ncustom-config) kernels in practice (and this should be possible with\nkernels for any distribution, or vanilla ones) that include core\nXarray support, but do not have CONFIG_ZONE_DEVICE (or\nCONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE, which also selects CONFIG_XARRAY_MULTI)\nset, so CONFIG_XARRAY_MULTI is not set either, which causes the build\nto fail at the configure stage.\n\nReinstate the previous autoconf test, that detected the presence of\nXArray support in the kernel via a compilation test of xa_is_value(),\nin order to address this issue.\n\nHPE-bug-id: LUS-13525\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: ad66011dbd (\"LU-19179 compat: use directly native Xarray...\")\nSigned-off-by: Nikitas Angelinas <nikitas.angelinas@hpe.com>\nChange-Id: I812001f7c83fe05a382ea305f4ae979ca06fed66\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
